\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Per-image advantage $A=L_{\mathrm  {base}}-L_{\mathrm  {super}}$ distribution on the validation sets. Both are concentrated near zero with a long positive tail---most frames gain little from the deep path while a minority gain a lot. The tail is wider on KITTI ($\sigma {=}0.21$) than on BDD100K ($\sigma {=}0.10$).}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:adv_dist}{{7}{7}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces  Runtime latency-budget tracking under realistic scene-condition drift on BDD100K MOT, run as a live on-device closed loop. Sequences are concatenated in alternating condition order (night$\leftrightarrow $daytime, city$\leftrightarrow $highway, clear$\leftrightarrow $rainy; rows), with shaded bands marking each segment's condition. A PI controller adjusts the router threshold $\tau $ to hold a step (left) and a sawtooth (right) latency budget $L^\star (t)$ (black dashed); the realized mean latency (red) tracks it with MAE $0.18$--$0.30$\,ms across all condition drifts. }}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:budget}{{8}{8}{}{}{}}
