\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IV}{\ignorespaces  TensorRT FP16 engine-switching overhead on the embedded Jetson Orin Nano (pure GPU inference, CUDA-event timed, $1000$ iterations after warm-up), reported at two input resolutions to span compute scales. \textsc  {alternating} forces a BASE$\leftrightarrow $SUPER engine switch on every frame (per-frame worst case); at both resolutions its latency stays within $0.2\%$ of the mean of the two static single-path engines, so routing between two resident engines is effectively free. Resident GPU memory (FP16 weights $+$ activation scratch) is reported per engine; the router is negligible. }}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
